1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Preserve the UI. Partition the state.
Keep one deal column and N product columns. Apollo owns remote data. Shared values live once; independent product fields live in small proxies.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:23,000
How an isolated field update works
A typed action mutates one product proxy. Its access-tracked snapshot updates the subscribed input. Other product proxies receive no subscription notification.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Shared fields and deal summaries
Linked inputs read one shared proxy. Broadcasts are explicit commands. Derive summaries or maintain counts in commands; avoid two-way synchronization effects.

4
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Advantages
Corrected Valtio keeps the existing programming style. Narrow subscriptions are efficient; no replacement library is required to fix state ownership.

5
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Disadvantages
The library does not enforce good boundaries. Broad snapshots, duplicated values, and unmanaged effects can bring the original problems back.

6
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:12,000
When I would choose it
Valtio remains a defensible choice. Preserve canonical fields, typed commands, virtualization, and lifecycle cleanup regardless of the library.
